  "description": "A fast mathematics parsing engine for .NET. It supports expression nesting, variables, custom functions and all standard mathematical operations for integer, decimal (floating point), logic and bitwise. Expressions are compiled once and evaluated without allocating, and nulls are supported.\n      In addition to custom functions and variables, these are built in: abs, acos, asin, atan, atan2, avg, ceil, clamp, cos, cosh, count, deg, e, exp, floor, hypot, if, log, log10, logn, max, min, modpow, not, pi, pow, prod, rad, rand, round, sign, sin, sinh, sqrt, sum, tan, tanh, trunc.",
  "iconFile": "128.png",
  "id": "NTDLS.ExpressionParser",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-10-08T02:35:37.807Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
