  "packageHash": "BC6U4Wv6C6NyYTj0xPsqqCxJ4ttEeGXclwMN8p11MetRigwNXVy/uE1OWGoEYt5ojSQImvl4ZoqyNyma7E5zSA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 99722,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/NTDLS/NTDLS.ExpressionParser",
  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Rewritten engine: expressions are parsed and compiled in a single pass to a program that evaluates without allocating (~44 ns with variables, ~0.5 μs to parse and evaluate a new expression).\n      New: OperationCount, the == operator, unary ~ (bitwise NOT), show work lists every operation, and no limit on nesting depth.\n      Many parsing bugs fixed, including variables replaced inside function names, functions without parameters, negated groups and variables, signs after comparisons, decimal precision, and operands separated only by whitespace.\n      Behavior changes: operator precedence now follows C, syntax errors are thrown by the constructor, show work has a new format, and malformed input (e.g. \"a b\", \"a < = b\", \"max(1,)\", \"$\") is rejected.\n      See the release notes on GitHub for details.",
